      "message": "An hourly charge below the National Living Wage (£12.71 an hour from 1 April 2026 for workers aged 21 and over) cannot cover lawful pay and on-costs. HMRC treats this as a warning sign of non-compliance in the supply chain. The charge does not set anyone's pay, but check the Supplier can pay lawfully.",
